# Food Swipe -- Supabase environment configuration
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com/dashboard (free tier is fine).
#   2. In your project: Project Settings -> API, copy the "Project URL" and
#      the "anon public" API key into the two values below.
#   3. Apply the SQL migrations in supabase/migrations/ to your project,
#      either by pasting each file's contents into the Supabase Dashboard's
#      SQL Editor and running them in order (0001, then 0002), or, if you
#      have the Supabase CLI installed and linked to this project, by
#      running `supabase db push` from the project root.
#   4. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values below. `.env` is
#      gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Astro only exposes environment variables prefixed with PUBLIC_ to
# client-side code (see https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/environment-variables/).
# The anon key is safe to expose to the browser -- it is designed for that --
# as long as Row Level Security policies (see supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql)
# are enabled on every table, which they are in this project.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
